    \  gives: Whole numbers have no fixed width. Adding, subtracting and multiplying them never overflows and never\
    \ loses\n    a digit, however large they grow.\n  example: 18446744073709551615 plus 1 is 18446744073709551616,\
    \ exactly; a total past two to the sixty-third is\n    kept.\n  stated:\n  - in: python\n    version: 3.13.18\n\
