    \ code\n- id: C:reliance/number-from-text\n  type: reliance\n  name: a whole number read from text\n  summary:\
    \ A whole number is read from text that may have spaces, tabs or line ends around it, a plus or minus sign,\n\
    \    single underscores between digits, leading zeros, and the decimal digits of any script, not only 0 to 9.\n\
    \  stance: observed\n  'on': language\n  gives: A whole number is read from text that may have spaces, tabs\
    \ or line ends around it, a plus or minus sign,\n    single underscores between digits, leading zeros, and the\
    \ decimal digits of any script, not only 0 to 9. Anything\n    else is refused.\n  example: ''' 5_0'', ''+7'',\
    \ ''007'' and the Arabic-Indic digit seven are read as 50, 7, 7 and 7; ''5__0'' and\n    ''1.0'' are refused.'\n\
